.TH VERITAS 1 "2026" "veritas 0.10.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
veritas \- discover and run Veritas test suites, tests and benchmarks
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B veritas
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B veritas
is the command line interface of the Veritas unit, integration and black box
testing framework for GNU Guile.
.PP
It walks a project looking for test files, loads each file's entry point and
runs it.  By default the entry point is a no-argument function called
.BR spec ,
files are looked up under
.B ./test
and test modules are expected to be named
.BR "(veritas unit ...)" .
.PP
Every option is a thin syntactic sugar over a
.B VERITAS_*
environment variable.  The command line therefore produces exactly the same
configuration as setting the environment by hand, which keeps local runs,
CI pipelines and programmatic runs reproducible and in sync.
.PP
Every run ends with its totals: one line names how many test files ran and how
many suites, tests and assertions they held between them.  With
.BR \-\-jobs
the counts of the workers are merged, so the line describes the whole run and
not one process of it.
.PP
A file that fails does not end the run.  The files after it still run, the
failures are named together at the end, and the run exits 1 once every file has
had its turn.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-scan\-dir " " DIR
Root directory scanned for tests
.RB ( VERITAS_SCAN_DIR ,
default
.BR ./ ).
.TP
.BR \-T ", " \-\-test\-top\-dir " " DIR
Directory holding the test hierarchy
.RB ( VERITAS_TEST_TOP_DIR ,
default
.BR test ).
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-test\-type " " TYPE
Test category and sub-directory to load
.RB ( VERITAS_TEST_TYPE ,
default
.BR unit ).
.TP
.BR \-e ", " \-\-entrypoint " " NAME
No-argument function called inside every test file
.RB ( VERITAS_ENTRYPOINT ,
default
.BR spec ).
.TP
.BR \-m ", " \-\-test\-module " " NAME
Top level module prefix of the tests
.RB ( VERITAS_TEST_MODULE ,
default
.BR veritas ).
.TP
.BR \-r ", " \-\-reporter " " NAME
Reporter to use
.RB ( VERITAS_REPORTER ,
default
.BR emoji-reporter ).
Other built-in choices include
.BR monotone-reporter ,
.B json-reporter
and
.BR junit-reporter ,
the last of which writes a JUnit XML report at the end of the run
.RB ( VERITAS_JUNIT_PATH ,
default
.BR reports/junit/veritas-junit.xml ).
.TP
.B \-\-only\-test " " SUBSTR
Only run tests whose name contains
.IR SUBSTR
.RB ( VERITAS_ONLY_TEST ).
.TP
.B \-\-only\-suite " " SUBSTR
Only run suites whose name contains
.IR SUBSTR
.RB ( VERITAS_ONLY_SUITE ).
.TP
.B \-\-only\-tag " " TAG
Only run tests and suites carrying
.IR TAG
.RB ( VERITAS_ONLY_TAG ).
.TP
.B \-\-only\-failed
Rerun only the tests recorded as failing by the previous run
.RB ( VERITAS_ONLY_FAILED=true ).
.TP
.B \-\-no\-only\-failed
Ignore the recorded failures (the default).
.TP
.BR \-\-seed " " N
Seed every shuffle of the run, which replays the order a shuffled run reports
.RB ( VERITAS_SEED ).
.TP
.BR \-\-partition " " I/T
Run slice
.I I
of the
.I T
slices of the discovered test files
.RB ( VERITAS_PARTITION ).
.TP
.BR \-j ", " \-\-jobs " " N
Run the discovered test files in
.I N
worker processes, one file per process.  Their output is streamed in file order
as it is written - the earliest file that has not been printed in full is the
only one shown, so the log reads as a single-process run's would - and their
records of failures, their JUnit reports and their counts are merged
.RB ( VERITAS_JOBS ).
.TP
.B \-\-coverage
Measure code coverage and write the LCOV trace, the JSON summary and the HTML
report
.RB ( VERITAS_COVERAGE ).
.TP
.B \-\-no\-coverage
Do not measure coverage (default).
.TP
.BR \-\-coverage\-dir " " DIR
Directory the LCOV trace and the JSON summary are written to, defaults to
.BR reports/lcov
.RB ( VERITAS_COVERAGE_DIR ).
.TP
.BR \-\-coverage\-html\-dir " " DIR
Directory the HTML report is written to, defaults to
.BR reports/html ;
the value
.B false
turns the HTML report off
.RB ( VERITAS_COVERAGE_HTML_DIR ).
.TP
.BR \-\-coverage\-include " " DIRS
Colon-separated source roots the report is limited to, defaulting to the current
directory
.RB ( VERITAS_COVERAGE_INCLUDE ).
.TP
.BR \-\-coverage\-exclude " " DIRS
Colon-separated source roots left out of the report
.RB ( VERITAS_COVERAGE_EXCLUDE ).
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-shuffle
Shuffle the order of discovered files (default;
.BR VERITAS_SHUFFLE_FILES=true ).
.TP
.B \-\-no\-shuffle
Keep the discovered file order
.RB ( VERITAS_SHUFFLE_FILES=false ).
.TP
.BR \-b ", " \-\-benchmarks
Run benchmarks (default;
.BR VERITAS_RUN_BENCHMARKS=true ).
Benchmarks always run sequentially so that the profiler produces sound
measurements.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-benchmarks
Skip benchmarks
.RB ( VERITAS_RUN_BENCHMARKS=false ).
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Display a help page and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Display version information and exit.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B VERITAS_ENTRYPOINT
Entry point function name.  Defaults to
.BR spec .
.TP
.B VERITAS_SCAN_DIR
Directory to scan for tests.  Defaults to
.BR ./ .
.TP
.B VERITAS_TEST_TYPE
Test type directory.  Defaults to
.BR unit .
.TP
.B VERITAS_TEST_TOP_DIR
Test hierarchy root.  Defaults to
.BR test .
.TP
.B VERITAS_TEST_MODULE
Module prefix of the test suites.  Defaults to
.BR veritas .
.TP
.B VERITAS_SHUFFLE_FILES
Either
.B true
or
.BR false .
Defaults to
.BR true .
.TP
.B VERITAS_RUN_BENCHMARKS
Either
.B true
or
.BR false .
Defaults to
.BR true .
.TP
.B VERITAS_ONLY_TEST
Optional substring filter on test names.
.TP
.B VERITAS_ONLY_SUITE
Optional substring filter on suite names.
.TP
.B VERITAS_ONLY_TAG
Optional tag filter.  A test or suite runs when any of its tags contains the
value, case-insensitively.
.TP
.B VERITAS_ONLY_FAILED
Either
.B true
or
.BR false .
When true, only the tests named in
.B reports/last-failed.scm
run; every run rewrites that file with the names that failed, or with an empty
list when everything passed.
.TP
.B VERITAS_SEED
Seed for every shuffle of the run.  A shuffled run prints the seed it drew, and
setting this variable to that value reproduces the order.
.TP
.B VERITAS_PARTITION
Either unset or
.IR INDEX/TOTAL ,
for example
.BR 2/3 .
The discovered files are sorted and split round-robin, and only that slice runs.
A malformed or impossible value is an error.
.TP
.B VERITAS_JOBS
Number of worker processes used for the discovered test files.  Defaults to
.BR 1 ,
which runs them in the process that discovered them; higher values spread the
files over that many processes.  A file that fails exits only its own worker, so
every file still runs and the runner exits 1 when any of them failed.
.TP
.B VERITAS_COVERAGE
Either
.B true
or
.BR false .
When true, every test file the runner loads is measured, whether or not it asks
for coverage with
.BR #:with-coverage? .
When false, nothing is measured, even a file that asks: an explicit refusal
beats a file's own default.
The LCOV trace and the JSON summary go to
.B VERITAS_COVERAGE_DIR
and the HTML report to
.BR VERITAS_COVERAGE_HTML_DIR .
.TP
.B VERITAS_COVERAGE_DIR
Directory the LCOV trace and the JSON summary are written to.  Defaults to
.BR reports/lcov .
.TP
.B VERITAS_COVERAGE_HTML_DIR
Directory the HTML report is written to.  Defaults to
.BR reports/html ;
.B false
turns it off.
.TP
.B VERITAS_COVERAGE_INCLUDE
Colon-separated source roots the report is limited to.  Defaults to the current
directory, which keeps Guile and the other dependencies out of the report.
.TP
.B VERITAS_COVERAGE_EXCLUDE
Colon-separated source roots left out of the report.  Nothing is excluded by
default.
.TP
.B VERITAS_COBERTURA_PATH
Where the Cobertura XML document is written.  Defaults to
.B coverage.xml
next to the LCOV trace.
.TP
.B VERITAS_JACOCO_PATH
Where the JaCoCo XML document is written.  Defaults to
.B jacoco.xml
next to the LCOV trace.
.TP
.B VERITAS_LAST_FAILED_PATH
Where a run records the names of the tests that failed.  Defaults to
.BR reports/last-failed.scm ;
a run split over worker processes writes one record per worker and merges them
into this path.
.TP
.B VERITAS_SNAPSHOT_DIR
Directory snapshots are written to and read from.  Defaults to
.BR test/snapshots .
.TP
.B VERITAS_UPDATE_SNAPSHOTS
Either
.B true
or
.BR false .
When true, the snapshots a run reaches are rewritten instead of compared.
.TP
.B VERITAS_JUNIT_PATH
Where the JUnit XML report is written when the reporter is
.BR junit-reporter .
Defaults to
.BR reports/junit/veritas-junit.xml .
.TP
.B VERITAS_REPORTER
Reporter symbol.  Defaults to
.BR emoji-reporter .
The built-in choices are
.BR emoji-reporter ,
.BR monotone-reporter ,
.B json-reporter
and
.BR junit-reporter .
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
All selected tests and benchmarks finished successfully.
.TP
.B 1
A test failed, an option was invalid, or an error occurred while loading or
running the tests.
.SH EXAMPLES
Run the unit tests with the project defaults:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
veritas
.EE
.RE
.PP
Run the integration suite, without benchmarks, keeping file order:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
veritas \-t integration \-\-no\-benchmarks \-\-no\-shuffle
.EE
.RE
.PP
Use the plain reporter and only run suites mentioning
.BR auth :
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
veritas \-r monotone\-reporter \-\-only\-suite auth
.EE
.RE
.PP
Rerun what failed last time, then replay a failing order:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
veritas \-\-only\-failed
veritas \-\-seed 42
.EE
.RE
.PP
Run one third of the test files, and write a JUnit XML report:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
veritas \-\-partition 1/3
veritas \-r junit\-reporter
veritas \-\-jobs 4
.EE
.RE
.PP
Measure coverage of the sources, leaving the tests out of the report:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
veritas \-\-coverage \-\-coverage\-exclude test
.EE
.RE
.PP
Inside a Guix development shell:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
guix shell \-m manifest.scm \-\- ./bin/veritas \-h
.EE
.RE
.SH INTERACTIVE USE
The same runner is available from a Guile REPL.  Load the CLI module to
inspect or reuse its configuration:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
(use\-modules (veritas cli))
(show\-help)
(run\-cli '("--test\-type" "unit"))
.EE
.RE
.PP
To run with the current environment without parsing a command line, call the
runner directly:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
((@ (veritas runner) run\-tests))
.EE
.RE
